invariant: INV-13
file: src/tcp_read.c
catches: tcp_nonblocking_loop_test
reason: ch_read_in_place waits on a header whose length field is above what
  RFC 9846 §5.2 lets a record hold, so a caller waits for a body no peer
  may send and the session stays live; INV-13 admits CH_TCP_AGAIN only for
  a record that can still arrive.

--- old
    if (body > rec_body_max(outer)) {
        w->alert = ALERT_RECORD_OVERFLOW; // RFC 9846 §5.2 caps the length (rfc9846.txt:3595-3596)
        return CH_EPROTO;
    }
--- new
    if (body > rec_body_max(outer)) {
        return CH_TCP_AGAIN;
    }
